  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Dry weather continues into the end of October.\n\nA dry cold frontal passage this evening into tonight will barely\nbe noticeable other than an increase in cloud cover along and \nbehind the front. High pressure builds into the region again \nbehind the front for tomorrow as a pronounced ridge develops \nover the eastern US. This will keep dry conditions around \nthrough at least the beginning of next week with seasonably warm\ndays and chilly nights. \n\nHREF probs of temperatures falling below freezing Friday night \nare around 50 percent for Lancaster and Lebanon Counties (the \nonly zones where the growing season remains active). This is \nsupported by the NAM MOS guidance which shows temperatures right\naround 32 in both of those counties. This information, combined\nwith the very favorable set up for efficient radiational \ncooling, has given us enough confidence to issue a Freeze Watch\nfor Friday night/Saturday morning.",
